   "source": [
    "```{ojs}\n",
    "//| echo: false\n",
    "datos    = transpose(datos_olap)\n",
    "regiones = [...new Set(datos.map(d => d.region))].sort()\n",
    "tiempos  = [...new Set(datos.map(d => d.tiempo))].sort()\n",
    "productos = [...new Set(datos.map(d => d.producto))].sort()\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Slice\n",
    "\n",
    "Fija una dimensión en un valor único. El subcubo resultante conserva las dos dimensiones restantes y muestra su distribución de ventas.\n",
    "\n",
    "```{ojs}\n",
    "viewof slice_dim = Inputs.radio(\n",
    "  [\"tiempo\", \"region\", \"producto\"],\n",
    "  {label: \"Dimensión fija\", value: \"tiempo\"}\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "viewof slice_val = Inputs.select(\n",
    "  slice_dim === \"tiempo\"   ? tiempos   :\n",
    "  slice_dim === \"region\"   ? regiones  : productos,\n",
    "  {label: \"Valor\"}\n",
    ")\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "```{ojs}\n",
    "//| echo: false\n",
    "slice_resto    = [\"region\", \"tiempo\", \"producto\"].filter(d => d !== slice_dim)\n",
    "slice_filtrado = datos.filter(d => d[slice_dim] === slice_val)\n",
    "\n",
    "slice_agg = Array.from(\n",
    "  d3.rollup(\n",
    "    slice_filtrado,\n",
    "    v  => d3.sum(v, d => d.ventas),\n",
    "    d  => d[slice_resto[0]],\n",
    "    d  => d[slice_resto[1]]\n",
    "  ),\n",
    "  ([a, m]) => Array.from(m, ([b, ventas]) => ({\n",
    "    [slice_resto[0]]: a,\n",
    "    [slice_resto[1]]: b,\n",
    "    ventas\n",
    "  }))\n",
    ").flat()\n",
    "\n",
    "Plot.plot({\n",
    "  title:  `Slice — ${slice_dim} = \"${slice_val}\"`,\n",
    "  color:  {legend: true, label: slice_resto[0]},\n",
    "  x:      {label: slice_resto[1]},\n",
    "  y:      {label: \"Ventas (100K MXN)\", grid: true},\n",
    "  fx:     {label: slice_resto[0]},\n",
    "  width:  680,\n",
    "  height: 280,\n",
    "  marks: [\n",
    "    Plot.barY(slice_agg, {\n",
    "      x:    slice_resto[1],\n",
    "      y:    \"ventas\",\n",
    "      fill: slice_resto[0],\n",
    "      fx:   slice_resto[0],\n",
    "      tip:  true\n",
    "    }),\n",
    "    Plot.ruleY([0])\n",
    "  ]\n",
    "})\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "```{ojs}\n",
    "//| echo: false\n",
    "Inputs.table(slice_agg, {sort: \"ventas\", reverse: true})\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Roll-up y Drill-down\n",
    "\n",
    "Cambia el nivel de agregación de la dimensión geográfica. Seleccionar *Zona* aplica un **roll-up** que agrupa regiones; volver a *Región* aplica un **drill-down** que recupera el detalle.\n",
    "\n",
    "```{ojs}\n",
    "viewof nivel_geo = Inputs.radio(\n",
    "  [\"Región  (drill-down)\", \"Zona  (roll-up)\"],\n",
    "  {label: \"Nivel geográfico\", value: \"Región  (drill-down)\"}\n",
    ")\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "```{ojs}\n",
    "//| echo: false\n",
    "zona_map = new Map([\n",
    "  [\"Norte\",     \"Zona Norte-Centro\"],\n",
    "  [\"Centro\",    \"Zona Norte-Centro\"],\n",
    "  [\"Occidente\", \"Zona Occidente-Sureste\"],\n",
    "  [\"Sureste\",   \"Zona Occidente-Sureste\"]\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "datos_geo = nivel_geo.startsWith(\"Zona\")\n",
    "  ? datos.map(d => ({...d, region: zona_map.get(d.region)}))\n",
    "  : datos\n",
    "\n",
    "geo_agg = Array.from(\n",
    "  d3.rollup(\n",
    "    datos_geo,\n",
    "    v  => d3.sum(v, d => d.ventas),\n",
    "    d  => d.region,\n",
    "    d  => d.tiempo\n",
    "  ),\n",
    "  ([region, m]) => Array.from(m, ([tiempo, ventas]) => ({region, tiempo, ventas}))\n",
    ").flat()\n",
    "\n",
    "Plot.plot({\n",
    "  title:  nivel_geo.startsWith(\"Zona\")\n",
    "            ? \"Roll-up — ventas por zona geográfica y trimestre\"\n",
    "            : \"Drill-down — ventas por región y trimestre\",\n",
    "  color:  {legend: true, label: \"Región / Zona\"},\n",
    "  x:      {label: \"Trimestre\"},\n",
    "  y:      {label: \"Ventas (100K MXN)\", grid: true},\n",
    "  fx:     {label: nivel_geo.startsWith(\"Zona\") ? \"Zona\" : \"Región\"},\n",
    "  width:  680,\n",
    "  height: 280,\n",
    "  marks: [\n",
    "    Plot.barY(geo_agg, {\n",
    "      x:    \"tiempo\",\n",
    "      y:    \"ventas\",\n",
    "      fill: \"region\",\n",
    "      fx:   \"region\",\n",
    "      tip:  true\n",
    "    }),\n",
    "    Plot.ruleY([0])\n",
    "  ]\n",
    "})\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dice\n",
    "\n",
    "Selecciona subconjuntos en dos o más dimensiones al mismo tiempo. Desmarcar opciones reduce el subcubo; la gráfica y la tabla se actualizan en tiempo real.\n",
    "\n",
    "```{ojs}\n",
    "viewof dice_reg  = Inputs.checkbox(regiones,  {label: \"Regiones\",    value: regiones})\n",
    "viewof dice_tpo  = Inputs.checkbox(tiempos,   {label: \"Trimestres\",  value: tiempos})\n",
    "viewof dice_prod = Inputs.checkbox(productos, {label: \"Productos\",   value: productos})\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "```{ojs}\n",
    "//| echo: false\n",
    "dice_filtrado = datos.filter(d =>\n",
    "  dice_reg.includes(d.region)   &&\n",
    "  dice_tpo.includes(d.tiempo)   &&\n",
    "  dice_prod.includes(d.producto)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "dice_agg = Array.from(\n",
    "  d3.rollup(\n",
    "    dice_filtrado,\n",
    "    v  => d3.sum(v, d => d.ventas),\n",
    "    d  => d.region,\n",
    "    d  => d.producto\n",
    "  ),\n",
    "  ([region, m]) => Array.from(m, ([producto, ventas]) => ({region, producto, ventas}))\n",
    ").flat()\n",
    "\n",
    "dice_agg.length > 0\n",
    "  ? Plot.plot({\n",
    "      title:  \"Dice — subcubo seleccionado\",\n",
    "      color:  {legend: true, label: \"Producto\"},\n",
    "      x:      {label: \"Producto\", axis: null},\n",
    "      y:      {label: \"Ventas (100K MXN)\", grid: true},\n",
    "      fx:     {label: \"Región\"},\n",
    "      width:  680,\n",
    "      height: 280,\n",
    "      marks: [\n",
    "        Plot.barY(dice_agg, {\n",
    "          x:    \"producto\",\n",
    "          y:    \"ventas\",\n",
    "          fill: \"producto\",\n",
    "          fx:   \"region\",\n",
    "          tip:  true\n",
    "        }),\n",
    "        Plot.ruleY([0])\n",
    "      ]\n",
    "    })\n",
    "  : html`<p style=\"color:gray;font-style:italic\">\n",
    "      Selecciona al menos un valor en cada dimensión para ver resultados.\n",
    "    </p>`\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "```{ojs}\n",
    "//| echo: false\n",
    "dice_agg.length > 0\n",
    "  ? Inputs.table(dice_agg, {sort: \"ventas\", reverse: true})\n",
    "  : html``\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "## Agregaciones y medidas derivadas\n",
    "\n",
    "Las medidas de un cubo pueden ser simples o derivadas. Una medida simple es la suma de ventas; una medida derivada puede ser participación porcentual, crecimiento trimestral o margen. En OLAP conviene distinguir entre medidas aditivas, semi-aditivas y no aditivas [@kimball2013data].\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.callout-note appearance=“minimal”}\n",
    "Definición. Una medida aditiva puede agregarse mediante suma a lo largo de todas las dimensiones relevantes del cubo.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "M(A\\cup B)=M(A)+M(B),\\qquad A\\cap B=\\varnothing\n",
    "$$\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "Las ventas son usualmente aditivas: se pueden sumar por producto, región y tiempo. En cambio, una tasa de conversión no debe agregarse sumando porcentajes; debe recalcularse a partir de numeradores y denominadores.\n",
    "\n",
    "El siguiente ejemplo calcula ventas totales por producto y participación porcentual dentro del total."
   ]
